AnoGraph's sources use std::max/min and std::numeric_limits without including
the headers that declare them. It compiled for its authors on an older libstdc++
that pulled <algorithm> in transitively; on the ubuntu image it does not.

This was three `sed -i '1i ...'` lines in the Dockerfile. `git apply` is not
cosmetic here: sed inserts blindly, so after a SOURCE_REF bump that adds the
include upstream it would silently produce a duplicate, while git apply refuses
a patch whose context no longer matches and the build stops with a diagnostic.

Applies to SOURCE_REF=6e8bcd85a39ac49de01ea58d4d15690add8f69c8.

